        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 23:26:36.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lod: keep default LMV pool for subdirectories",
        "message": "LU-21061 lod: keep default LMV pool for subdirectories\n\nA default LMV that names a pool keeps a subtree on the MDTs of the\npool only for as many levels as it is inherited: the default given\nto a new subdirectory is rebuilt without the pool, it is dropped\nonce max_inherit runs out, and with implicit inheritance it is not\nstored on the subdirectory at all.\n\nCopy the pool into the default LMV of a new subdirectory.  When the\nparent default stops inheriting, give the subdirectory a default\nwith only the pool, a single stripe on any MDT of the pool and\nunlimited inheritance.  Store the default of a new subdirectory if\nit has a pool, also with implicit inheritance, so that the MDT can\nfind the pool of the directory.  A pool that lists only OSTs is kept\nthe same way, so that new files deep in the tree stay on its OSTs;\nsubdirectories there are then placed by space usage rather than\nalways on the parent MDT.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I4d94ccb96b6c066f1bb7fd0a945d93856cb7218b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
